2019 (v0.1.0 - Inception):

Initial concept designs and planning of the command-based API architecture on paper.

Writing the initial core code structure using Python and Ursina.

Fundamentals of basic object creation commands.

2020 - 2021 (v0.2.0 - Movement & Transforms):

Adding functions for moving, rotating, and scaling entities.

Establishing the basic loop system for processing keyboard inputs.

2022 - 2023 (v0.3.0 - Scene & Stage Architecture):

Adding structures that manage in-game level/scene transitions.

Making the codebase more modular and simplified.

2024 - Present (v1.0.0 - Public Release):

Bringing the project to the open-source world and officially placing it on GitHub under the MIT license.
